# Commit Message Offer

After completing code changes (unless the user already asked you to commit), end the reply with a ready-to-paste commit message they can use.

## Format

1. Short section titled `Commit message` (or similar).
2. A single fenced `text` block containing only the message body (no `git commit` wrapper unless they asked to commit).
3. Follow repo style: concise, focus on **why**, complete sentences, no em/en dashes.
4. Match recent `git log` tone when known (imperative or descriptive is fine if consistent with the branch).

## Example

```text
Commit message

fix: replace latin-1 separator in GithubConnectCard so Nuxt Docker builds accept UTF-8.
```

## When not to

- Read-only questions with no file changes.
- User already requested a commit in the same turn (then create the commit instead).
- No changes remain (already committed / nothing to commit).
